{number: 21}
{title: I’ve Found a Friend, oh, Such a Friend}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] I've found a Friend, oh, [C] such a Friend!
He [G] loved me ere I [D] knew Him;
He [G] drew me with the [C] cords of love,
And [G] thus He bound me [D7] to [G] Him.
And [D] round my heart still [G] closely twine
Those [C] ties which naught can [D] sever,
For [G] I am His, and [C] He is mine,
For-[G] ever and for-[D7] ev-[G] er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] I've found a Friend, oh, [C] such a Friend!
He [G] bled, He died to [D] save me;
And [G] not alone the [C] gift of life,
But [G] His own self He [D7] gave [G] me.
Naught [D] that I have my [G] own I'll call,
I'll [C] hold it for the [D] Giver;
My [G] heart, my strength, my [C] life, my all,
Are [G] His, and His for-[D7] ev-[G] er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] I've found a Friend, oh, [C] such a Friend!
All [G] power to Him is [D] given,
To [G] guard me on my [C] onward course,
And [G] bring me safe to [D7] hea-[G] ven.
The [D] eternal God is [G] my refuge,
And [C] underneath are [D] ever
The [G] everlasting [C] arms of love:
His [G] arms that fail me [D7] nev-[G] er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[G] I've found a Friend, oh, [C] such a Friend!
So [G] kind, and true, and [D] tender,
So [G] wise a Counselor [C] and Guide,
So [G] mighty a De-[D7] fen-[G] der!
From [D] Him, Who loves me [G] now so well,
What [C] power my soul can [D] sever?
Shall [G] life or death, or [C] earth or hell?
No; [G] I am His for-[D7] ev-[G] er.
{end_of_verse}
